---
import Default from "../layouts/Default.astro";
---

<Default
  title="TinyGPT — an open-source LLM factory and runtime that lives on your Mac"
  description="Distill routed specialists, package them for MLX, and know exactly where they fail. Train, fine-tune (LoRA / DoRA / QLoRA), evaluate (BFCL / τ-bench / lm-eval), serve OpenAI-compatible, and inspect with SAE / MEMIT / patch — all on one Apple Silicon machine. MIT licensed. Built in the open by one developer."
  ogTitle="TinyGPT — an open-source LLM factory that lives on your Mac"
  ogDescription="Distill, fine-tune, evaluate, serve, and inspect LLMs on a single Mac. Runs in a browser tab too. MIT."
  twitterTitle="TinyGPT — an open-source LLM factory that lives on your Mac"
  twitterDescription="Distill, fine-tune, evaluate, serve, and inspect LLMs on a single Mac. Runs in a browser tab too. MIT."
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <header class="topbar" role="banner">
    <a class="brand-lockup" href="/" aria-label="TinyGPT home">
      <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">T</span>
      <span class="brand-name">TinyGPT</span>
    </a>
    <nav class="topnav" aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="/playground">playground</a>
      <a href="/leaderboard">leaderboard</a>
      <a href="/devlog">devlog</a>
      <a href="/roadmap">roadmap</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/sarthak-fleet/tinygpt" rel="noopener">github</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="landing" id="main">
    <!-- ========== HERO ========== -->
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-h1">
      <p class="hero-kicker">An open-source LLM factory for one Mac.</p>
      <h1 id="hero-h1">
        Build routed specialists that earn their keep &mdash;
        <span class="highlight">on a laptop you already own.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        TinyGPT is a Swift codebase + 30&plus; CLI subcommands for the full
        post&#8209;training stack on Apple Silicon: train, distill from a local
        teacher, fine&#8209;tune with LoRA / DoRA / QLoRA, gate with real evals
        (BFCL, &tau;&#8209;bench, lm&#8209;eval), serve OpenAI&#8209;compatible,
        and open the model up with sparse autoencoders, MEMIT, activation
        patching. Same model also trains and runs in a browser tab via
        hand&#8209;written WebGPU kernels. The first packaged specialist is
        honest by design: frontier&#8209;level on file&#8209;ops, routed only because
        it regresses outside that domain.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="cta primary" href="https://github.com/sarthak-fleet/tinygpt#build-it-locally" rel="noopener">
          <span class="cta-label">Build the Mac CLI</span>
          <span class="cta-sub"><code>xcodebuild</code> &middot; macOS 14+ &middot; MLX&#8209;Swift</span>
        </a>
        <a class="cta secondary" href="/playground">
          <span class="cta-label">Open the browser playground</span>
          <span class="cta-sub">WebGPU &middot; trains a GPT&#8209;2 in your tab</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="hero-fineprint">
        MIT&nbsp;licensed &middot; one&nbsp;developer, building&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;open &middot;
        no cloud, no API key, nothing leaves the laptop.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ========== THE NUMBER ========== -->
    <section class="number-card" aria-labelledby="num-h2">
      <p class="num-eyebrow">The strongest measured claim</p>
      <h2 id="num-h2" class="num-h2">
        A 4B routed file&#8209;ops specialist, locally distilled, matches the
        frontier on its multi&#8209;turn hard gate.
      </h2>

      <div class="num-figure">
        <div class="num-figure-left">
          <span class="num-hero" aria-hidden="true">100<span class="num-pct">%</span></span>
          <span class="num-hero-label">Qwen3&#8209;4B file&#8209;ops specialist</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="num-bars" aria-label="Multi-turn hard gate, task-completion rate by model">
          <li>
            <span class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-label">DeepSeek&#8209;V4&#8209;pro <span class="bar-tag">frontier</span></span>
              <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="--w:100%"></span></span>
              <span class="bar-value">100<span class="pct">%</span></span>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="is-us">
            <span class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-label">Qwen3&#8209;4B file&#8209;ops specialist <span class="bar-tag bar-tag-accent">tinygpt</span></span>
              <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill bar-fill-accent" style="--w:100%"></span></span>
              <span class="bar-value">100<span class="pct">%</span></span>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-label">Gemma&#8209;4&#8209;12B&#8209;qat</span>
              <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="--w:83%"></span></span>
              <span class="bar-value">83<span class="pct">%</span></span>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-label">Qwen3&#8209;4B (stock&nbsp;+&nbsp;plan&nbsp;prompt)</span>
              <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="--w:75%"></span></span>
              <span class="bar-value">75<span class="pct">%</span></span>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-label">Gemma&#8209;3&#8209;12B</span>
              <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="--w:33%"></span></span>
              <span class="bar-value">33<span class="pct">%</span></span>
            </span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="num-caption">
        BFCL multi&#8209;turn hard gate, n=12 GorillaFileSystem agentic tasks,
        task&#8209;completion rate. Distillation: ~99 frontier trajectories &times;
        LoRA SFT, single Mac, no cloud train. Cheap routed specialist&nbsp;&gt;&nbsp;bigger general
        on one domain is the project thesis &mdash; not "4B&nbsp;&gt;&nbsp;12B in general."
        The same file&#8209;ops specialist regresses on out&#8209;of&#8209;domain breadth
        (60&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;42%), so TinyGPT packages it with the caveat instead of
        pretending it is a general planner.
        <a href="/docs/learn/tool-calling-frontier-parity">Full writeup, including the honest tradeoffs &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ========== NUMBERS STRIP ========== -->
    <section class="metrics" aria-labelledby="metrics-h2">
      <h2 id="metrics-h2" class="section-h2">Measured, on one Mac.</h2>
      <p class="section-blurb">
        Numbers below are from a stock M5 Pro / 48 GB. Reproducible via
        <code>tinygpt bench</code> and the linked artefacts. Where a number
        applies only to a specific preset or build, the preset is named.
      </p>

      <dl class="metric-grid">
        <div class="metric">
          <dt>Decode throughput</dt>
          <dd><span class="m-val">696</span><span class="m-unit">tok/s</span></dd>
          <p class="m-note">Huge preset, 221M params. 293&nbsp;tok/s on the 960M Mega pilot.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <dt>TTFT warm</dt>
          <dd><span class="m-val">5.8</span><span class="m-unit">ms</span><span class="m-pct">p99</span></dd>
          <p class="m-note">Cold start: 24&nbsp;ms on a 1B model. ITL p99: 4.9&nbsp;ms.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <dt>Training step</dt>
          <dd><span class="m-val">42</span><span class="m-unit">ms</span></dd>
          <p class="m-note">Huge preset, 17.2&times; the same model in&#8209;browser via WebGPU.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <dt>WebGPU vs WASM SIMD</dt>
          <dd><span class="m-val">12.1</span><span class="m-unit">&times;</span></dd>
          <p class="m-note">At d_model=256. Scales 2.6&times;&rarr;12.1&times; as d_model grows 96&rarr;256.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <dt>ANE M8 decode</dt>
          <dd><span class="m-val">17</span><span class="m-unit">tok/s</span></dd>
          <p class="m-note">28&#8209;block Qwen3 chain on the Apple Neural Engine, layer&#8209;chunked Core ML.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <dt>Largest fit</dt>
          <dd><span class="m-val">960</span><span class="m-unit">M</span></dd>
          <p class="m-note">Params trainable end&#8209;to&#8209;end on unified memory; 473M in a browser tab via Memory64.</p>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <!-- ========== THE LOOP ========== -->
    <section class="loop" aria-labelledby="loop-h2">
      <h2 id="loop-h2" class="section-h2">The loop the runtime closes.</h2>
      <p class="section-blurb">
        Each surface emits the input the next one needs. The agent runtime
        records token&#8209;preserving trajectories; those trajectories become
        SFT data; that data trains the next specialist; the eval gate decides
        whether it ships.
      </p>

      <ol class="pipeline" role="list">
        <li class="step" data-step="01">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <span class="step-name">Data</span>
          <span class="step-cmd">tinygpt download&#8209;dataset</span>
          <span class="step-detail">22 curated sets. HF streaming, Magpie synth, GitHub issue&rarr;PR, MS&#8209;MARCO, the&#8209;stack&#8209;smol.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="step" data-step="02">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <span class="step-name">Distill</span>
          <span class="step-cmd">tinygpt distill</span>
          <span class="step-detail">KL&nbsp;+&nbsp;NLL teacher&rarr;student. Local teacher (Qwen3, Gemma, DeepSeek via API or Codex CLI). Rejection&#8209;sample on a checker.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="step" data-step="03">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <span class="step-name">Train / SFT / DPO</span>
          <span class="step-cmd">tinygpt sft &middot; dpo &middot; es</span>
          <span class="step-detail">Full PEFT bundle: LoRA, LoRA+, DoRA, VeRA, LoftQ, AdaLoRA, RsLoRA, PISSA. DPO/SimPO/KTO/ORPO in one trainer.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="step" data-step="04">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <span class="step-name">Eval gate</span>
          <span class="step-cmd">tinygpt eval&#8209;gate</span>
          <span class="step-detail">BFCL, &tau;&#8209;bench, lm&#8209;eval (MLX adapter), HumanEval+sandbox, judge shim. Exit&#8209;non&#8209;zero on regression.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="step" data-step="05">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <span class="step-name">Serve</span>
          <span class="step-cmd">tinygpt serve</span>
          <span class="step-detail">OpenAI&nbsp;+&nbsp;Ollama surfaces on the same socket. Continue.dev / any OpenAI client plugs in unchanged.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="step" data-step="06">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
          <span class="step-name">Agent</span>
          <span class="step-cmd">tinygpt agent</span>
          <span class="step-detail">Multi&#8209;turn, tool dispatch, persistent KV, FSM&#8209;constrained JSON, optional <code>&#8209;&#8209;cloud&#8209;escalate</code>.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="step step-loop" data-step="07">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
          <span class="step-name">Traces &rarr; data</span>
          <span class="step-cmd">tinygpt traces&#8209;to&#8209;data</span>
          <span class="step-detail">Every rollout is a token&#8209;preserving <code>.atraj</code>. Filter, dedupe (MinHash), emit ChatML SFT JSONL. Then loop to step&nbsp;02.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ========== PILLARS ========== -->
    <section class="pillars" aria-labelledby="pillars-h2">
      <h2 id="pillars-h2" class="section-h2">What ships, audited against the code.</h2>
      <p class="section-blurb">
        PLAN.md is the canonical shipped/skipped/TODO ledger. Each pillar
        below is one subset; clicking through gets you to specific files
        and the papers each technique cites.
      </p>

      <div class="pillar-grid">
        <article class="pillar">
          <header>
            <span class="pillar-tag">Train</span>
            <h3>Every modern pre/post&#8209;train, one trainer.</h3>
          </header>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Pretrain</strong> &mdash; byte&#8209;level or BPE; WSD schedule, gradient checkpointing, spike recovery</li>
            <li><strong>SFT</strong> &mdash; response&#8209;only masking, ChatML / Alpaca / Llama / plain</li>
            <li><strong>Preference</strong> &mdash; DPO, SimPO, KTO, ORPO (one trainer, flags)</li>
            <li><strong>PEFT</strong> &mdash; LoRA, LoRA+, DoRA <em>(TGLA v2 on disk)</em>, VeRA, LoftQ, AdaLoRA, RsLoRA, PISSA, LoRA&#8209;FA</li>
            <li><strong>Optimisers</strong> &mdash; AdamW, Lion, Sophia, Muon, Adafactor, GaLore</li>
            <li><strong>Architecture</strong> &mdash; RoPE+GQA, sliding window, ALiBi, MoE, MoD, differential attn, YOCO, MTP</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar">
          <header>
            <span class="pillar-tag">Distill</span>
            <h3>Frontier teacher &rarr; small student.</h3>
          </header>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>KL&nbsp;+&nbsp;NLL</strong> mix loss with temperature and &alpha; (Hinton 2015)</li>
            <li><strong>Rejection&#8209;sampled</strong> trajectories &mdash; keep only what a checker passes</li>
            <li><strong>Gold&#8209;clone fallback</strong> &mdash; on verifiable tasks the gold IS the trajectory; teacher&#8209;free reproduces the same model</li>
            <li><strong>Trace replay</strong> &mdash; render in the student's own chat template via <code>render_sft_from_traj.py</code></li>
            <li><strong>Headline result</strong> &mdash; 4B at frontier&#8209;parity, <a href="/docs/learn/tool-calling-frontier-parity">documented honestly</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar">
          <header>
            <span class="pillar-tag">Eval</span>
            <h3>Where the moat is.</h3>
          </header>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Shared schema</strong> &mdash; every eval emits the same JSONL row (E0)</li>
            <li><strong>tinygpt eval&#8209;bfcl</strong> &mdash; 10 BFCL categories, OpenAI&#8209;compat shim into <code>tinygpt&nbsp;serve</code></li>
            <li><strong>tinygpt eval&#8209;tau&#8209;bench</strong> &mdash; retail + airline, configurable user simulator</li>
            <li><strong>tinygpt run&#8209;lm&#8209;eval</strong> &mdash; MLX adapter for <code>lm&#8209;evaluation&#8209;harness</code>, two modes</li>
            <li><strong>tinygpt eval&#8209;humaneval</strong> &mdash; Rust&nbsp;+&nbsp;<code>sandbox&#8209;exec</code> code execution</li>
            <li><strong>tinygpt eval&#8209;gate</strong> &mdash; CI&#8209;grade regression gate, exits non&#8209;zero</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar">
          <header>
            <span class="pillar-tag">Serve &middot; Agent</span>
            <h3>OpenAI&#8209;compatible. Locally.</h3>
          </header>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>tinygpt serve</strong> &mdash; OpenAI <em>and</em> Ollama on the same socket; Continue.dev provider compat</li>
            <li><strong>tinygpt agent</strong> &mdash; multi&#8209;turn loop, tool dispatch, persistent KV, FSM JSON</li>
            <li><strong>&#8209;&#8209;cloud&#8209;escalate</strong> &mdash; defer to Anthropic / OpenAI only when the local model wants to</li>
            <li><strong>Speculative decoding</strong> &mdash; vanilla, Medusa, EAGLE&#8209;2 (trainable heads)</li>
            <li><strong>StreamingLLM sink</strong>, KV&#8209;cache quant (KIVI), prefix caching</li>
            <li><strong>Token&#8209;preserving traces</strong> &mdash; <code>.atraj</code> rollouts feed next round of SFT</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar">
          <header>
            <span class="pillar-tag">Interp</span>
            <h3>Open the model up.</h3>
          </header>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Logit lens</strong> &middot; <strong>tuned lens</strong> (trainable per&#8209;layer probes)</li>
            <li><strong>Activation patching</strong> &mdash; zero + donor&#8209;swap, on (layer, position)</li>
            <li><strong>Per&#8209;layer ablation</strong> &middot; <strong>attention heatmap</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Linear probes</strong> &mdash; trainable per&#8209;layer classifiers, <code>.lp</code> sidecar</li>
            <li><strong>ROME</strong> &middot; <strong>MEMIT</strong> &mdash; rank&#8209;1 and rank&#8209;K fact editing, multi&#8209;layer with key&#8209;norm weighting</li>
            <li><strong>Sparse autoencoders</strong> &mdash; <code>tinygpt sae</code>, group&#8209;SAE, SAELens / Neuronpedia export</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="pillar pillar-browser">
          <header>
            <span class="pillar-tag pillar-tag-warm">In a browser tab</span>
            <h3>The same model, no install.</h3>
          </header>
          <p class="pillar-prose">
            Hand&#8209;written WGSL kernels train a GPT&#8209;2 in your tab.
            Blocked 4&times;4 matmul (5.18&times; kernel speedup at 2048&sup3;), FA2
            forward&nbsp;+&nbsp;backward in WGSL, Memory64 lifts the 4&nbsp;GB tab
            heap so a 473M&#8209;param model allocates cleanly.
            End&#8209;to&#8209;end parity vs. the WASM reference: &le;&nbsp;2.5%
            loss drift.
          </p>
          <p class="pillar-cta">
            <a class="inline-cta" href="/playground">Open the playground &rarr;</a>
            <span class="inline-cta-divider" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
            <a class="inline-cta inline-cta-quiet" href="/speedup">See the speedup curve &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ========== RUN IT ========== -->
    <section class="run" aria-labelledby="run-h2">
      <h2 id="run-h2" class="section-h2">Run it.</h2>
      <p class="section-blurb">
        Two paths. The Mac path is the primary one; the browser path is for
        when you want everything in&#8209;tab, no toolchain, no install.
      </p>

      <div class="run-grid">
        <article class="run-card run-card-primary">
          <header>
            <h3>On a Mac</h3>
            <p class="run-tag">macOS 14+ &middot; Xcode &middot; Apple Silicon &middot; MLX&#8209;Swift</p>
          </header>
          <pre class="code-block" aria-label="Mac quickstart commands"><code><span class="cm"># build the CLI</span>
cd native&#8209;mac
export DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer
xcodebuild -scheme tinygpt -destination 'platform=macOS,arch=arm64' \
  -derivedDataPath .xcode-build build

<span class="cm"># one&#8209;command quickstart: data &rarr; specialist &rarr; chat</span>
tinygpt quickstart --data my.jsonl

<span class="cm"># or distill from a local teacher</span>
tinygpt distill --teacher qwen3-4b --student huge \
  --data ./traces --out ./student.tinygpt

<span class="cm"># then serve it OpenAI&#8209;compatible</span>
tinygpt serve --model ./student.tinygpt --port 8080</code></pre>
          <p class="run-card-cta">
            <a class="inline-cta" href="https://github.com/sarthak-fleet/tinygpt#build-it-locally" rel="noopener">Full build instructions &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="run-card">
          <header>
            <h3>In a browser tab</h3>
            <p class="run-tag">WebGPU &middot; Chrome 113+ / Safari 18+ &middot; no install</p>
          </header>
          <p class="run-prose">
            The playground builds a transformer in WebAssembly + WebGPU,
            trains it in a Web Worker so the UI never freezes, and lets you
            watch the loss curve live as the model picks up structure.
            Every interpretability surface above is wired in &mdash;
            attention heatmap, logit lens, ablation, patching &mdash; under
            one "Inspect &amp; evaluate" panel.
          </p>
          <ul class="run-bullets">
            <li>Parity&#8209;tested against the WASM reference to &le;&nbsp;2.5% loss drift</li>
            <li>OPFS checkpoint persistence &mdash; a run survives a tab refresh</li>
            <li>Capability detection picks the right preset for your machine</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="run-card-cta">
            <a class="inline-cta" href="/playground">Open the playground &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ========== HONEST SCOPE ========== -->
    <section class="honest" aria-labelledby="honest-h2">
      <h2 id="honest-h2" class="section-h2">Honest scope.</h2>
      <div class="honest-grid">
        <div class="honest-col">
          <h3>What this is</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A single&#8209;developer project, shipping in public, MIT.</li>
            <li>Mac&#8209;first &mdash; M&#8209;series, unified memory, MLX&#8209;Swift.</li>
            <li>A factory for <em>specialists</em>, not a general assistant.</li>
            <li>An OpenAI&#8209;compatible runtime any client already speaks.</li>
            <li>A research substrate for interp, eval, and distillation.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="honest-col">
          <h3>What this isn&rsquo;t (yet)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              A general&#8209;skill specialist. The frontier&#8209;parity 4B
              dropped on out&#8209;of&#8209;domain BFCL (60&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;42%) &mdash;
              real catastrophic forgetting. Mixed&#8209;backend distillation
              is the documented fix.
            </li>
            <li>Multi&#8209;GPU or distributed training. One device, single Mac.</li>
            <li>A cloud product. Nothing leaves the laptop unless <code>&#8209;&#8209;cloud&#8209;escalate</code> is set.</li>
            <li>An enterprise platform. No SSO, no tenancy, no SLA.</li>
            <li>A finished story. The <a href="/roadmap">roadmap</a> shows what&rsquo;s shipped and what&rsquo;s next.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ========== LEARN ========== -->
    <section class="learn" aria-labelledby="learn-h2">
      <h2 id="learn-h2" class="section-h2">Read the journey.</h2>
      <p class="section-blurb">
        Decision logs and per&#8209;technique explainers; each ties back to
        the paper it cites and the file where it lives.
      </p>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/learn/tool-calling-frontier-parity">
          <span class="doc-title">Tool&#8209;calling: frontier&#8209;parity at 4B</span>
          <span class="doc-sub">The headline result, the distillation recipe, and the honest tradeoffs</span>
        </a>
        <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/PLAN">
          <span class="doc-title">PLAN.md &mdash; shipped &middot; skipped &middot; TODO</span>
          <span class="doc-sub">The canonical ledger, audited against the code</span>
        </a>
        <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/distillation">
          <span class="doc-title">Knowledge distillation</span>
          <span class="doc-sub">KL + NLL mix loss, temperature, &alpha;, rejection sampling</span>
        </a>
        <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/training/index">
          <span class="doc-title">Three phases of training</span>
          <span class="doc-sub">Pretrain &rarr; SFT &rarr; DPO with paste&#8209;ready commands</span>
        </a>
        <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/interpretability">
          <span class="doc-title">Interpretability tools</span>
